==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|it}} {{term|brunus|brūnus|lang=la}} "brown, brunet" (whence also {{etyl|es|-}} {{term|bruno|lang=es}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|brun|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|frk|it}} *{{term||brūn|lang=frk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|it}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*brūnaz||brown}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|it}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*bher-||shining, brown}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|brun|brūn|lang=goh}} "brown" ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|braun|lang=de}} "brown"), {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|brun|brūn|lang=ang}} "brown". More at {{l/en|brown}}.

===Adjective===
{{it-adj|brun}}

# (dark) [[brown]]

====Derived terms====
* [[orso bruno]]

===Noun===
{{it-noun|brun|m|o|i|f=bruna|fpl=brune}}

# a dark-haired person

